  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development of a biopsychosocial translational research programme in post-traumatic stress disorder.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Deliver significant research funding for internationally competitive and innovative collaborative projects between researchers from Colombia and United Kingdom that will allow the pursuit of shared research interests.
ODA statement says: The violence in Colombia is related to high levels of PTSD and associated co-morbidities that have transcending impacts on poverty dynamics and individual economic decisions in the country. The program we propose will provide a great deal of clarity on the mental health needs within the region and on a wide variety of biological, social, and psychological risk and resilience factors. Through participation 500 people will be offered psychosocial support, where required, with effective and efficient psychological therapies. Here we propose integrating research and mental health care to benefit patients recruited to the study. Our program will therefore facilitate access to treatment for recruited patients, thus offering mental health care for a population exposed to armed conflict in Cesar, Colombia which has very limited access to such care.&#x202f;
Through a synergistic collaboration between the UK and Colombia, we will investigate the mechanisms underlying PTSD in a population long exposed to Colombian armed conflict, that also represents a significant gap in the population coverage of currently published PTSD studies.
 This project relies on the unique partnership in Colombia (ICC in Cesar) This collaboration will bring together expertise in high-throughput genetic approaches (UK) and cutting-edge gene editing technologies to Colombia to better understand PTSD, and contribute to our understanding of its mechanisms and susceptibility factors. By involving graduate students and training them in areas that will ensure their future competitiveness, we will contribute to training, career development, and transfer of knowledge between collaborators from both countries.
Public engagement is also an important objective of the proposed work. We will contribute to both countries&#x2019; science education, which addresses current educational concerns in Colombia and the UK. All PIs will participate in local outreach events for science education in their home institutions and in Cesar, Colombia.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
